{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"role\": \"workshop\",\n  \"verdict\": \"APPROVE\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.95,\n  \"summary\": \"The plugin implements the FM-12 'Camel Gate' logic to prevent agent turns from ending while background tasks are active without a scheduled wakeup. It correctly maps tool-based task creation (including argument-specific flags), settlement via terminal status patterns, and wakeup scheduling. The state management is per-agent and correctly handles turn transitions and a fail-open steering cap to prevent infinite loops.\",\n  \"concerns\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C1\",\n      \"section\": \"lib/index.js:113\",\n      \"description\": \"The `settleTools` logic depends on `resultText` concatenating content. If a tool result returns structured data that is not specifically 'text' type blocks, the terminal status regex might fail to find the status line even if the job is settled.\",\n      \"severity\": \"non_blocking\",\n      \"recommended_fix\": \"Ensure the `resultText` helper or the regex is robust against different result content structures if `dsh-tool-jobs` evolves.\",\n      \"investigation_task\": \"Verify if `dsh-tool-jobs` always outputs the terminal status line as a text block in the result content array.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"closed_prior_concerns\": [],\n  \"search_findings\": \"N/A - Source code analysis performed on provided target files.\",\n  \"niyyah_audit\": {\n    \"honorsSource\": true,\n    \"guardsFailureMode\": true,\n    \"note\": \"The implementation specifically addresses the 2026-08-24 lifecycle bug regarding permanent gate opening.\"\n  }\n}\n```"}}
